# Pairs with HandOffBound. Moved from the design's
# ReadPositionHonestRearmWithoutReplay. The design let the owner re-arm as soon as
# the marker closed, without replaying to the close heads. The replay itself is
# the core module's; this module's half of the guard is that the close records the
# heads to replay to. Here the marker keeps the previous close's heads, so a
# foreign append of this window lies at or above them.
MODULE: HandOffBoundRearmWithoutReplay
TARGET: HandOffBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the close closes the marker without recording its heads, so the owner has nothing to replay to
PERTURBS: Close

--- FIND
    /\ fFence' = fEpoch + 1
    /\ hoClosedAt' = next
    /\ hoOpen' = FALSE
--- REPLACE
    /\ fFence' = fEpoch + 1
\* MUTATION: the close records no heads; the marker keeps the last close's.
    /\ hoClosedAt' = hoClosedAt
    /\ hoOpen' = FALSE
--- END
